WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.220
<b>Townsfolks'
Emergency Shelter</b>

38
00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.890
What's wrong? The mayor's never
been gone for this long before.

39
00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:57.890
I hope he's all right.

40
00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.390
It sounded like a battle
was going on in town.

41
00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.900
There's been a lot more
cannon fire than usual, today.

42
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.980
I'll go to town to check it out.

43
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.320
You all just stay here.

44
00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.900
I'm going with you.

45
00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:09.610
No way.

46
00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:11.740
There are still pirates in town.

47
00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.450
It's too dangerous of a situation.

48
00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.910
Yes, Exactly. That's why
you'll need our help.

49
00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:17.580
What kind of citizens are we

50
00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.450
if we don't help?

51
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.660
We have got to find
out what's happening!

52
00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.410
You can't stop us from going.

53
00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.790
We wanna do all we can to help out.

54
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:27.590
Then it's settled.

55
00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:29.550
We all go together!

56
00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:40.720
<b>Pirate Buggy "the Clown"</b>

57
00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:40.560
In all my life, I've never
been as mad at someone as him!

58
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.480
That bastard, Shanks, stole
countless riches from me!

59
00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:49.110
I don't know how you two are connected,
but I can say whatever I want about him!

60
00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.820
I've earned that!

61
00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:57.530
The North Pole!

62
00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.410
South Pole!

63
00:02:58.410 --> 00:02:59.740
That's what you say!

64
00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:02.830
Right, and I'm gonna keep on
saying it because I'm right, clown!

65
00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:04.370
Oh, you got guts!

66
00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.960
I'm gonna settle this once and for all!

67
00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.130
Go ahead and try!

68
00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:08.290
All right, you bastard!

69
00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.170
I'm gonna bust you up flashily!

70
00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.500
Counter attack!

71
00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.760
Knock it off!

72
00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.550
Nobody but you two cares which is
colder, the North Pole or the South.

73
00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.850
If you wanna know so badly, then why
don't you go to both and find out!

74
00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.060
Now cool it!

75
00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.100
A ship!

76
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:22.970
Huh?

77
00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.770
Enemy ship to the north-northeast!

78
00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.520
Right! Get ready! Time to fight!

79
00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:29.770
Yes sir!

80
00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.150
Yes... I can't wait to plunder!

81
00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:33.820
You seem happy, Buggy.

82
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:34.990
Obviously!

83
00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:37.910
Enemy ships are just like
big floating treasure chests.

84
00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.870
It's only natural for
pirates to raid 'em!

85
00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.160
Am I wrong?

86
00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.910
Well, there's some truth to that.

87
00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.080
You're too weak!

88
00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.160
You and everyone else
here just don't have

89
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.540
the pirate's natural hunger and
desire for plundering treasure!

90
00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:55.050
You don't know what
it means to be a pirate!

91
00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.010
What's this?!

92
00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.680
It's... a... treasure map!

93
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.730
I've never seen one before!

94
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.640
It's incredible!

95
00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.980
Is the treasure on the
bottom of the ocean?

96
00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.980
Yes!

97
00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:20.820
Now my life's path is
flashily decided!

98
00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.800
Hey, Buggy!

99
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.510
Aren't you gonna come
celebrate with us?

100
00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:37.130
We found a whole lot
of really neat stuff.

101
00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.010
It's no map!

102
00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.050
I... don't have... anything hidden...

103
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:41.220
Go away!

104
00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.050
What are you talking about, Buggy?

105
00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.760
Oh, uh, nothing.

106
00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.980
You said you were gonna
leave this ship sometime, right?

107
00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.940
So, what do you plan to do?

108
00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.780
I'm gonna get my own ship, then gather
a reliable crew and see the world.

109
00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.660
I'm gonna take my time. Heh...
All as a pirate, of course.

110
00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:06.160
What a bunch of sentimental nonsense!

111
00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.120
Say what?!

112
00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.830
I do admire your
fighting skill, though.

113
00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:14.210
If you weren't such a softy,
I'd make you one of my henchmen.

114
00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.210
Your henchman?

115
00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.090
Heh, I don't think so.

116
00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:18.010
Huh?

117
00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:20.220
We have completely different
outlooks on life,

118
00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:22.800
so I think we should just
follow our own paths.

119
00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.890
That's what pirates do.

120
00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:27.350
Heh! You think you're such
an expert on pirates.

121
00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:31.520
But if we ever meet on the ocean,
and we'd have to have a fight to the death.

122
00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.520
Yeah... Pirates do that, too.

123
00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.280
You never make sense.

124
00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.900
Anyways, you said something about
finding some interesting loot, right?

125
00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.910
Huh? Oh yeah, We found a Devil Fruit.

126
00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:44.320
A Devil Fruit?

127
00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.910
I heard that the different fruits
are incarnations of the Sea Devil.

128
00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.200
Supposedly, if you eat one,

129
00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:53.960
you gain devil powers but the sea will
hate you and take your ability to swim.

130
00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.960
You'd have to be stupid
to eat that thing!

131
00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.970
I'd never get that treasure on
the ocean floor if I couldn't swim!

132
00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:02.930
But still...

133
00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:07.140
I bet you could sell that fruit for
at least a hundred million berries.

134
00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:08.930
Heh...

135
00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:10.100
What?!

136
00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.930
I, pirate apprentice Buggy,

137
00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:15.060
am about to devour this Devil Fruit!

138
00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:17.690
You gotta love the kids.

139
00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.530
Never thinking of consequences.

140
00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.870
Well, Buggy?

141
00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:27.870
Do you feel any differently yet?

142
00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.240
No... Not really...

143
00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.500
Aww, was it a fake?

144
00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:32.410
I'm not surprised.

145
00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:36.040
I've never seen a real
Devil Fruit before.

146
00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.260
Yes! That worked flashily well!

147
00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.970
These guys are so gullible.

148
00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:47.010
I can't believe I was able to
trick them so easily.

149
00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.640
Now, to jump ship before
they find out the truth!

150
00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.100
With the money I get from selling this
Devil Fruit and finding the sunken treasure,

151
00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.400
I'll easily be able to form
my own crew.

152
00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:57.650
Hey there, Buggy!

153
00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:59.400
Were you just saying something?

154
00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:00.650
Oh, it's you!

155
00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:01.980
Don't scare me like that!

156
00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.320
Don't be so jumpy.

157
00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.320
And don't steal too much
food from the kitchen.

158
00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:07.990
You don't wanna make the cook mad!

159
00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.160
Whew, that was close...

160
00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:11.410
Oh yeah!

161
00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:12.910
The captain told me to tell ya...

162
00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.880
– Damn you, Bastard!
– Hey, what's wrong?

163
00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.670
Why? Why? Why?!

164
00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:25.970
What's that piece of paper?

165
00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:29.050
Ah! Not my map!

166
00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:30.890
Hey, Buggy!

167
00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:32.010
What the?

168
00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.100
W... What's going on?

169
00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.230
I can't move.

170
00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:39.360
Is it true that you lose
your ability to swim?!

171
00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.070
Damn it!

172
00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.900
Hey! Hey, What're you doin'?

173
00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:44.860
What's going on?

174
00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.400
Why aren't you swimming?

175
00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:48.780
Buggy!

176
00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.740
Help... Help me...

177
00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:56.040
I'll save you Buggy!

178
00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.800
So... are you telling me
that Shanks saved your life?

179
00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.300
No, that's not the point
I'm trying to get across!

180
00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.890
Because of what he did to
me I was unable to swim,

181
00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:15.350
and therefore unable to
obtain my sunken treasure!

182
00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:17.060
Then, I had a revelation!

183
00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:21.650
If I couldn't go underwater, then I'd
just obtain all the treasure on dry land!

184
00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:24.900
Using my brand new Chop-Chop Powers.

185
00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.860
And now I won't let anyone
who touches my treasure live!

186
00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:34.160
Death to those who try to
pilfer my hard earned treasure!

187
00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.160
Get back here you beast!

188
00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:40.750
Damn it! He spotted me!

189
00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:42.500
Hm?

190
00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.340
You don't stand a chance
of escaping from me!

191
00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:48.630
Now, I'm going to flashily chop you up!

192
00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:06.900
My balls... My balls...
That was a cheap shot!

193
00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.450
Don't run off yet, we're not done.

194
00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.360
Hey!

195
00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.160
You better drop that treasure
and get outta here, Nami.

196
00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.660
You don't want him
coming after you again.

197
00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:17.040
No!

198
00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.620
Drop the money and go?!

199
00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:19.500
No way!

200
00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.960
Why should I leave my treasure behind?

201
00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:25.460
Did you just call it your treasure?!

202
00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.210
That's right, you heard me!

203
00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:30.420
I'm a thief who steals from pirates,
and I just stole a lot of treasure

204
00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:32.430
from a really annoying one!

205
00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:35.390
So that makes this my
treasure now, Understand?!

206
00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.430
Ah! That makes sense!

207
00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.230
That's pure nonsense!

208
00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:42.390
That's my treasure and just
because you stole it from me

209
00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.150
doesn't make it yours,
you dirty, sneaky thief!

210
00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:48.730
Honestly! What did your
parents teach you?

211
00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:52.660
A criminal trying to lecture
another criminal? Ridiculous.

212
00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:53.950
What's that?!

213
00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:54.570
Hm?

214
00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.700
Whatever, the day I take
a morality lesson

215
00:09:57.330 --> 00:10:00.000
from you, is the day
I stop being a thief.

216
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.040
I hope you're ready
for the consequences.

217
00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:09.090
Now, Here comes, Chop, Chop...

218
00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:09.800
Huh?

219
00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:11.670
Festival!

220
00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:19.430
I'd like to see you try to save
your friend from me now, Gum-Gum!

221
00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:22.770
Damn it... He broke up
into smaller pieces!

222
00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.400
What the...?

223
00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:27.270
Nami?

224
00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:29.150
Give me back my treasure!

225
00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:30.230
No way!

226
00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.650
Huh?

227
00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.660
Coochie, coochi, coo!

228
00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:38.450
He,he...

229
00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.910
See how you like... this!

230
00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:45.790
Damn it! Knock it off!

231
00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.790
No, you knock it off!

232
00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.510
Whoa!

233
00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:57.930
Thanks for giving me my
treasure back, Nami.

234
00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:00.220
Let go!

235
00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:01.350
You, let go!

236
00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.230
This is my treasure so get
your grubby hands off it!

237
00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.730
Just give me back my treasure!

238
00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:11.650
Die!

239
00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:13.070
I already told you,

240
00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:15.570
You haven't finished
dealing with me yet!

241
00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.850
Consider that finishing move
a little gift from the old mayor guy!

242
00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.270
Thanks a lot, I owe you one.

243
00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:50.940
Sure! No problem.

244
00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.820
– Oh yeah! The map!
– My treasure!

245
00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:57.280
This isn't over yet, Gum-Gum!

246
00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.070
Ah! He's still alive!

247
00:11:59.070 --> 00:11:59.910
Shut up!

248
00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:03.910
How dare you flashily do this to me!

249
00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.210
You'll pay for this!

250
00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.710
Assemble, Chop-Chop Parts!

251
00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.970
Looking for these, Buggy?

252
00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:26.060
Gah! My parts!

253
00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.520
All right! Way to go thief!

254
00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:30.310
Stop it, now!

255
00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:32.190
See ya, Buggy!

256
00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:34.650
Now, Gum-Gum...

257
00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:36.190
Bazooka!

258
00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.630
I win!

259
00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:56.010
Whoa! That kid sure sent
Captain Buggy flyin'!

260
00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:59.170
So, What do we do
without the captain, huh?

261
00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.840
Keep acting unconscious.

262
00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:01.840
Good idea.

263
00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.140
Sorry your hat's all torn up.

264
00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.520
Don't worry, I can still put it on.

265
00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:14.570
And I got Buggy out of here,
so I'm satisfied for now.

266
00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:18.030
Bastard...

267
00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.780
When I have time, I'll fix
it for you, if you like.

268
00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.120
Huh? What's that?

269
00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.580
Oh forget it.

270
00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:29.120
I split this into two bags, so give
me a hand and carry half of it...

271
00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.370
It's too heavy for me.

272
00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.920
That sure is a lot.

273
00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:35.420
If anything, that clown
Buggy knew quality treasure

274
00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.670
when he saw it, and now it's all mine.

275
00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.880
I bet I can sell this for at
least ten million berries!

276
00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.350
Eh...

277
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:46.470
Here you go.

278
00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:47.310
Huh?

279
00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:49.140
It's the chart to the Grand Line.

280
00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:50.310
You do want it don't you?

281
00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:51.480
You're giving it to me?

282
00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:53.060
Because you saved my life.

283
00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:55.310
Ha! Thanks, Nami!

284
00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:58.980
Now I finally have it!
A map of the Grand Line!

285
00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.490
Hurray!

286
00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:03.660
Oh, does this also mean you'll
be joining me and my pirate crew?

287
00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:08.200
I told you, no matter what,
I'll never join a pirate crew!

288
00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.160
But, okay...

289
00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.040
Hanging around with you
seems profitable enough.

290
00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:16.630
Just remember this, I'm only joining
you... cause it's in my interest.

291
00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:18.300
Sure!

292
00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.510
Hey, Zoro! Wake up!

293
00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:23.680
Zoro!

294
00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:25.300
We're leaving!

295
00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.680
Did we take care of everything?

296
00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:31.520
Yeah! And we got a Navigator and
we got a chart of the Grand Line.

297
00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:33.350
Huh?

298
00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.730
Hmm.

299
00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:39.730
I'm not sure about this.
I feel light headed.

300
00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:42.740
Of course you do. It's
always something with you two.

301
00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:43.820
Honestly!

302
00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.450
Hey, wait a minute. What did I do?

303
00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.870
Are you kidding me?
You're the worst of them all!

304
00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.620
Anyways, let's go help the mayor.

305
00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.790
Oh, yeah.

306
00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:54.580
I guess we should wake the old
guy up, now that it's all over.

307
00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:55.710
– You there!
– Huh?

308
00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:57.920
You're not residents of this village!

309
00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.050
Nope. And who are you?

310
00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:02.260
What was all that cannon fire we heard?

311
00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:05.260
It sounded like there may
have been a battle here earlier.

312
00:15:05.260 --> 00:15:07.800
If you know anything, please tell us.

313
00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.890
Oh good, they're just citizens!

314
00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:12.220
I thought that maybe
they were more pirates.

315
00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.270
Oh, Mayor!

316
00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.980
Oh, no! Say something!

317
00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:15.980
Can you hear me?

318
00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:16.940
He's out cold.

319
00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:18.810
The pirates definitely did this.

320
00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.150
How horrible!

321
00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:23.190
No, I'm the one who
kicked that old man's ass.

322
00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:24.990
What?

323
00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:27.240
Hold on! You didn't have
to tell them that, did you?

324
00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:27.910
It's true.

325
00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:30.330
Maybe you should explain to them
so they don't get angry!

326
00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:37.040
Tell me, Why exactly did you knock our mayor
out and leave him in the street to die?

327
00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.210
You better explain yourselves!

328
00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:41.920
Who are you? Are you with the pirates?!

329
00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.170
They're getting really bloodthirsty.

330
00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:46.880
We can't let them know that
we're thieves and pirates.

331
00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:47.840
We're pirates.

332
00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.760
Just as we thought!

333
00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.770
– Idiot!
– But it's the truth!

334
00:15:55.770 --> 00:15:56.890
Pirates!

335
00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:59.150
How dare you ravage our town!

336
00:15:59.150 --> 00:16:02.570
We won't show you
any mercy for what you've done.

337
00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:03.650
What now?

338
00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.900
Doesn't look like they're
up for a discussion.

339
00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:09.240
Run!

340
00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.240
There's no escape!

341
00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.210
How dare you hurt our beloved mayor!

342
00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:23.800
How do you always make things worse?!

343
00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:24.840
This is a good town.

344
00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:25.710
Huh?

345
00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:29.340
Everyone's so mad, just
because of the old mayor guy!

346
00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:38.060
Something tells me they're not gonna
listen to our side of the story.

347
00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:39.020
We're turning here.

348
00:16:39.980 --> 00:16:42.150
Wait, hold on!
You gotta let me know sooner!

349
00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:43.570
They ran into the alley!

350
00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.190
Ha!

351
00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:44.940
Huh?

352
00:16:47.740 --> 00:16:49.860
Chouchou?!

353
00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.990
Doggie?!

354
00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.830
Hey! Move, Chouchou!

355
00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:57.830
Get outta here!

356
00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:00.250
Those three are pirates!

357
00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.750
You're barking at the wrong people!

358
00:17:03.920 --> 00:17:05.210
Why isn't he letting us pass through?!

359
00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.670
Chouchou, get outta here!

360
00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:12.590
Later, doggie!

361
00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.850
That was close.

362
00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.110
We only made it because of Chouchou.

363
00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:27.190
Why do we have to put up with this?

364
00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.610
Does it matter now?
We're done here anyway.

365
00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.450
\Yeah, Maybe so, but...

366
00:17:31.450 --> 00:17:33.530
Hey! Is this your boat?!

367
00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:34.870
It's great!

368
00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:37.490
It's nothing special,
but I guess it'll do.

369
00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.830
I stole it from some dumb
pirates a few days back.

370
00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.620
That's a big mouth you got!

371
00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:43.080
He! He!

372
00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.090
We been waitin' for
ya, ya little thief.

373
00:17:45.090 --> 00:17:47.920
Never thought you'd run into
us here, now didja, girlie?

374
00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.380
You know these guys?

375
00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:52.590
Yeah, sort of...

376
00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.550
Hey, It's not just sort of!

377
00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.100
We're bound together by fate!

378
00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.600
So, these are your friends.

379
00:17:57.600 --> 00:18:00.480
I guess we'll have to punish
the two of them as well.

380
00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:04.520
It's time you learned what happens
when you steal other people's stuff.

381
00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:08.860
Hey, you. Ya' hear me?
Time for your medicine. He. He.

382
00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:11.400
Huh?

383
00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:22.500
Hey, look! He's waking up!

384
00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.170
Ah... Thank goodness he's fine.

385
00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.880
What happened here, Mayor?

386
00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:31.380
What in the...

387
00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:34.430
It was like this when we got here...

388
00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:37.930
There were a few pirates when we
arrived, but they all ran off.

389
00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:41.270
Can you tell us what happened?

390
00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.930
Where are the young ones?

391
00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:46.650
What's that? Are you talking
about those three kids?

392
00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:50.530
So they're... still alive?!

393
00:18:50.530 --> 00:18:53.900
Those fools. Treating a
senior citizen like that.

394
00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:54.740
How rude.

395
00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:58.580
We drove those pirates
out of town, Mayor.

396
00:18:58.580 --> 00:19:00.700
You don't have to worry
about them anymore.

397
00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:02.080
But it's not enough.

398
00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:05.080
We have to make them pay for
what they've done to our village.

399
00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.500
They deserve to be punished
for destroying the peaceful

400
00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.170
town we all worked so hard to build.

401
00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:11.090
Yeah! She's right!

402
00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:12.760
There's still time to go after them.

403
00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:13.800
If we hurry...

404
00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:15.050
Shut your mouths!

405
00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:18.140
I'm the only one who's allowed
to complain about those kids!

406
00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:20.970
I won't let anyone else
bad-mouth them! You hear me?!

407
00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:24.100
What? Why are you protecting
those pirates, Mayor?

408
00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:27.520
Damn it! They think they can
just disappear and that's that?

409
00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.560
Where did they go?!

410
00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:31.980
Well... I think they were
running toward the port.

411
00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.440
Damn kids!

412
00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:38.410
They can't just leave like that!

413
00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:42.370
I have a lot of things I
want to say to you all!

414
00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.500
All right! Let's get going!

415
00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.960
Can I ask you somethin'?

416
00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:52.340
Isn't that Buggy's mark on your sail?

417
00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:54.170
Well this did used to be Buggy's boat.

418
00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:55.630
Think I should change it?

419
00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:59.930
Hey! Wait!

420
00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.180
Young ones!

421
00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.640
It's the old mayor guy.

422
00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:13.440
I was ready to die.

423
00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:16.740
I was ready to die,
filled with despair...

424
00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.070
Thanks! Thank you!

425
00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:26.000
Don't worry about it!

426
00:20:26.000 --> 00:20:27.660
Take it easy!

427
00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:32.590
Damn you, young ones.

428
00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:36.260
Damn you, young ones...

429
00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:38.180
I have no words...

430
00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:44.180
Huh?

431
00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:46.020
What'd you do, Luffy?! Huh?!

432
00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:48.440
Don't tell me you left that
bag of treasure back there!

433
00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:49.770
Yeah...

434
00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:51.980
That bag was worth around
five million berries, you idiot!

435
00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:55.690
That's right. And they're gonna need that
money to repair their destroyed town.

436
00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.820
But that was my treasure, jerk!

437
00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:01.070
Do you know how hard
I worked to steal it?!

438
00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:02.950
Why did you do that?

439
00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:04.660
Stop! I can't swim!

440
00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.240
That's the whole idea!

441
00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.750
If you want it,
just go back and get it, then!

442
00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.750
I can't do that! You go get it!

443
00:21:10.750 --> 00:21:12.710
No! That's dangerous!

444
00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:13.750
I could die, you know?!

445
00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:18.630
I don't care! And if you do that again,
I really will throw you in the ocean!

446
00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:25.600
Well, for better or worse, looks like
we finally have a navigator in our crew.

447
00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:39.590
As a kid I had a dream of a dazzling treasure

448
00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:46.610
I had a map in my head that I knew would lead me

449
00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:53.710
Charted a course all on my own so nobody would beat me

450
00:21:53.830 --> 00:22:00.970
The promised land was in my hand drew a line in the sand

451
00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:06.350
Look where I am

452
00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:14.760
My one ambitions slipping right through my hands

453
00:22:15.100 --> 00:22:22.030
But if the world ever changes Ill call out your name

454
00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:29.110
We could return to a time when our lives were still the same

455
00:22:29.240 --> 00:22:36.240
Take me to the place where memories remain

456
00:22:36.340 --> 00:22:42.110
Please dont ever let them fade
